{{Quote|''Skeleton Crew'' tells the story of four kids searching for their home planet after getting lost in the Star Wars galaxy, and the strange aliens and dangerous places they encounter on their adventure.|StarWars.com|<ref name="SW.com">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-skeleton-crew|text=''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''}}</ref>}}
'''''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''''' is a television series that premiered on [[Disney+]] on [[December 2]], [[2024]]. Starring [[Jude Law]] as [[Jod Na Nawood]] and focusing on four children in an adventure through the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[The galaxy|galaxy]] during the [[New Republic Era]], the live-action series was created and written by [[Jon Watts]] and [[Christopher Ford]]. ''Skeleton Crew'' features [[Wim]] ([[Ravi Cabot-Conyers]]), [[Fern]] ([[Ryan Kiera Armstrong]]), [[KB]] ([[Kyriana Kratter]]), [[Neel]] ([[Robert Timothy Smith]]), as well as the droid [[SM-33]] ([[Nick Frost]]) and the pirates [[Vane]], [[Brutus]], [[Chaelt]], [[Gunter]], and [[Pax (pirate)|Pax]]. It was announced on [[May 17]], [[2022]] under the code name '''''Grammar Rodeo''''' and its episodes were directed by Watts, [[David Lowery]], the Daniels ([[Daniel Kwan]] and [[Daniel Scheinert]]), [[Jake Schreier]], [[Bryce Dallas Howard]], and [[Lee Isaac Chung]]. The series is heavily influenced by the [[1985]] adventure film [[Wikipedia:The Goonies|''The Goonies'']].

==Official description==
''{{'}}''Star Wars'': Skeleton Crew{{'}}'' follows the journey of four kids who make a mysterious discovery on their seemingly safe home planet, then get lost in a strange and dangerous galaxy. Finding their way home—and meeting unlikely allies and enemies—will be a greater adventure than they ever imagined.''<ref name="ILM">{{ILM|url=vfx/star-wars-skeleton-crew|text=''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''}}</ref>''

==Development==
{{Quote|It's the story of their journey trying to find their way home. It stars four kids, but it is not a kids show.|Jon Watts|<ref name="Showcase">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-20-highlights-from-lucasfilms-studio-showcase|text=SWCA 2022: 20 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref>}}
On [[May 17]], [[2022]] [[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']] reported that a ''[[Star Wars]]'' series was in development for [[Disney+]], with [[Wikipedia:Spider-Man: No Way Home|''Spider-Man: No Way Home'']] director [[Jon Watts]] serving as creator and executive producer. [[Wikipedia:Spider-Man: Homecoming|''Spider-Man: Homecoming'']] writer [[Christopher Ford]] will serve as writer.<ref name="Vanity Fair" /> Later that month, during [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|Celebration Anaheim]], the name of the show and further details were revealed, including the casting of [[Jude Law]].<ref name="Showcase" /> [[Jon Favreau]] and [[Dave Filoni]], the creators of the shows [[Star Wars: The Mandalorian|''The Mandalorian'']] and ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka|Ahsoka]]'', which take place around the same time frame,<ref name="Showcase" /> are serving as executive producers.<ref name="Twitter" /> While filming ''Spider-Man: No Way Home'', Favreau asked Watts if he was interested in directing ''Star Wars''. Instead, Watts pitched his idea for a new series. Favreau called Filoni from [[Wikipedia:Atlanta|Atlanta]], and they joined a video call, where Watts pitched his idea.<ref name="Pitch">{{OfficialYouTube|channel=@entertainmentweekly|name=Entertainment Weekly|link=Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|video=M-RPU_Ceg4o|text=Jon Watts Pitched 'Skeleton Crew' To Jon Favreau On The Set Of 'Spider Man' #Shorts}}</ref> The series is heavily influenced by the [[1985]] children adventure film [[Wikipedia:The Goonies|''The Goonies'']] and other adventure stories of the era like [[Wikipedia:E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial|''E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial'']], [[Lucasfilm]]'s ''[[Indiana Jones (franchise)|Indiana Jones]]'' films and [[LucasArts]]'s video game [[Wikipedia:The Secret of Monkey Island|''The Secret of Monkey Island'']].<ref name="swcom creators interview">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-jon-watts-christopher-ford-interview|text=With ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'', Jon Watts and Chris Ford are Ready for Their Own Pirate Adventure}}</ref> It also feature references to the 1985 [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] film ''[[Ewoks: The Battle for Endor]]''<ref name="Teek">{{WebCite|url=https://www.empireonline.com/tv/news/star-wars-skeleton-crew-teek-ewok-battle-for-endor-exclusive|title=Star Wars: Skeleton Crew Will Bring Back The Teek From Ewok Movie The Battle For Endor|author=Ben Travis|work=[[Wikipedia:Empire (magazine)|''Empire'']]|date=2024-10-21|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/6LpPC}}</ref> and the [[1978]] ''[[The Star Wars Holiday Special]]''.<ref name="Circus holo">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-the-holiday-special|text=About that Circus Hologram in ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''&hellip;}}</ref>

The series soundtrack was composed by [[Mick Giacchino]].<ref name="Giacchino" /> The [[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew (Original Soundtrack)|soundtrack album]] was later released on [[January 17]], [[2025]].<ref name="Spotify">{{Spotify|url=album/1fMCKvCbTa4pul1633sH0K|text=Star Wars: Skeleton Crew (Original Soundtrack)}}</ref>

==Release and reception==
The series' first official trailer was released on [[August 10]], [[2024]].<ref name="Official Trailer 1">{{SWYouTube|a6voXgBlmpk|Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Streaming December 3 on Disney+}}</ref> ''Skeleton Crew'' was announced on [[May 26]], [[2022]] for a release in [[2023]],<ref name="Twitter" /> before later being moved to [[2024]].<ref name="Disney">{{Disney|subdomain=press|domain=co.uk|url=news/disney+-is-just-getting-started-non-stop-new-exclusives-coming-in-2024|text=DISNEY+ IS JUST GETTING STARTED: NON-STOP NEW EXCLUSIVES COMING IN 2024}}</ref> On August 10, 2024, it was announced that the series would be released on [[Disney+]] on [[December 3]], 2024.<ref name="Official Trailer 1" /> On [[November 27]] that year, the series' release date was moved earlier to [[December 2]], at 18:00 [[Wikipedia:Pacific Time Zone|PT]], with a two-episode premiere. They would be followed by a new episode every Tuesday until the final episode, episode 8, on [[January 14]], [[2025]].<ref name="Early">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-premiere-date|text=''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'' Will Debut Early|date=2024-11-26}}</ref>

A [[Huttese]] variation of the song "[[Wikipedia:Major Tom (Coming Home)|Major Tom (Coming Home)]]" by [[Wikipedia:Peter Schilling|Peter Schilling]] ([[1983]]) was used in the second trailer from [[November 1]],<ref name="Official Trailer 2">{{SWYouTube|f19gfOMZTtg|Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+}}</ref> and later received a full lyric video with the title "[[Youngee Wim (Bunky Dunko)]]."<ref name="Youngee Wim">{{SWYouTube|T2g4F3jNUdo|Skeleton Crew &#124; Youngee Wim (Bunky Dunko) Lyric Video &#124; Now Streaming on Disney+}}</ref>

===Accolades===
On [[November 18]], [[2025]], the series was nominated for 17 [[Wikipedia:Emmy Awards|Emmy Awards]] including "Outstanding Young Teen Series," "Outstanding Lead Performer in a Preschool, Children's or Young Teen Program" ([[Jude Law]]), "Outstanding Younger Performer in a Preschool, Children's or Young Teen Program" ([[Ravi Cabot-Conyers]]) and "Outstanding Writing for a Young Teen Series" ("[[This Could Be a Real Adventure]]").<ref name="Emmy Awards Nov 2025">{{DisneyCompany|url=children-family-emmy-award-nominations|text=The Walt Disney Company Dominates Across All Studios and Companies with Record-Breaking 103 Children’s & Family Emmy® Award Nominations}}</ref><ref name="SWNN Nov 2025">{{WebCite|url=https://www.starwarsnewsnet.com/2025/11/star-wars-skeleton-crew-young-jedi-adventures-and-rebuild-the-galaxy-all-recognized-in-the-children-family-emmy-nominations.html|text=‘Star Wars: Skeleton Crew,’ ‘Young Jedi Adventures,’ and ‘Rebuild the Galaxy’ All Recognized in the ‘Children & Family Emmy’ Nominations|author=Jay Goodearl|date=2025-11-19|work=Star Wars News Net|archivedate=20251124024633}}</ref>

